  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_022 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l, concat fusion) at 0.535 acc, which outperforms RNA-only (0.485) by ~5 points, confirming a small but real multimodal gain. Image-only performance is very weak (~0.21-0.23), suggesting the image contributes limited signal. Uncertainty: We have only tested concat fusion; it is unknown whether a weighted fusion strategy (which can down-weight the weaker image modality) would improve or degrade performance. This experiment (config_023) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_022, isolating the fusion strategy question. If weighted fusion improves accuracy, it indicates the modalities have asymmetric contributions and the weighting mechanism matters; if it performs similarly or worse, we can deprioritize fusion strategy and focus on other dimensions (multiprofile, alternative encoders). Under a tight budget, this minimal-change experiment maximizes information per trial by directly testing a high-impact design decision adjacent to our current best result."
}

